<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rupert I, Elector Palatine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1309">1309</a>–1390</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rupert I was count palatine of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, sole ruler from 1353, and the first of his line to hold the electoral dignity confirmed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-1356">Golden Bull of 1356</a>. He enlarged and consolidated the Palatinate on the Rhine and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neckar">Neckar</a> and in 1386 founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg-university">University of Heidelberg</a>, the oldest in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. His great-nephew became King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rupert-of-germany">Rupert of Germany</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rupert-i-elector-palatine.jpg" alt="Rupert I, Elector Palatine" width="268" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ruprecht_I_mit_Frauen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
